LUFS normalizer
---------------
Files:
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/lufs_normalizer.c
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/lufs_normalizer.h

The LUFS loudness targeting concept (K-weighted integrated-loudness
measurement over a sliding 400 ms window with a 100 ms step, and smooth
attack/release gain control towards a user target level) follows the
implementation in ViPERDSP, https://github.com/likelikeslike/ViPERDSP
(viper/effects/LUFSTargeting.cpp), a reverse engineering of ViPER4Android.

The original intellectual property of ViPER4Android belongs to Zhuhang and
ViPER520. ViPERDSP reverse engineering by Martmists, Iscle and likelikeslike
(https://github.com/AndroidAudioMods/ViPERFX_RE).

The loudness measurement itself implements the ITU-R BS.1770 method. The
K-weighting stages use the matched-biquad design published by Martin
Vicanek ("Matched Biquads") as formulated in libebur128,
https://github.com/jiixyj/libebur128 (MIT), which reproduces the standard's
published 48 kHz coefficient sets exactly at any sample rate. The relative
gate (-10 LU), silence-safe gain behaviour and the rootless/root
integration are this repository's own implementation.

This port remains under the GNU General Public License v3.0, like the rest of
this repository.

