These five effects are ported from RootlessViPER4Android,
https://github.com/alienware377/RootlessViPER4Android (viperextras.c and
viperextras2.c), which is itself distributed under the GNU General Public
License v3.0 and reimplements ViPER4Android effects as independent,
from-scratch DSP code.

The original intellectual property of ViPER4Android belongs to Zhuhang and
ViPER520.

Differences from the source required by this fork's spec: the effects are
reworked as standalone interleaved-buffer modules sharing one implementation
between the root effect and the rootless wrapper, and their sample-rate
dependent coefficients (compressor attack/release, Clarity shelf, AGC time
constants, Cure low-pass) are recomputed on sample-rate change instead of
keeping the rate current at parameter-set time. Parameter clamping at the
IPC trust boundary and the UI cards are this repository's own work.

This port remains under the GNU General Public License v3.0, like the rest of
this repository.

Vacuum tube saturation correction
---------------------------------
Files:
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/vacuumTube.c

The drive-stage saturation (asymmetric triode-like soft clipper applied in
the oversampled domain) and the partial makeup-gain compensation
(postgain = 1/pregain^0.6) are ported from RootlessViPER4Android,
https://github.com/alienware377/RootlessViPER4Android, which is itself
distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. Without it the drive
and the makeup gain cancelled each other exactly and the effect was a
mathematical no-op.

The original intellectual property of ViPER4Android belongs to Zhuhang and
ViPER520.

