this repository.

Engine safety fixes
-------------------
Files:
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/dbb.c
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/vdc.c
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/crossfeed.c
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/jdspController.c

The decimator phase reset (pos >= factor wrap and phase/buffer reset on
sample-rate change) is ported from RootlessViPER4Android,
https://github.com/alienware377/RootlessViPER4Android, which is itself
distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0. Without it a
48 kHz -> 44.1 kHz transition left the write position permanently past the
new factor and ran off the end of originalBuf (heap out-of-bounds).

The bounded DDC parser (per-section limits, exact sosCount*5 numbers per
section, strict rejection of malformed strings) is ported from the same
repository. Without it a number count that was not a multiple of five
(a trailing comma) wrote past the DirectForm2 arrays.

The convolver partition selector initializes the returned type to the
single-segment kind and clamps the benchmark-table index to the last entry
for block sizes above 32768, ported from the same repository. Without it an
uninitialized selection type or a table index of one past the end could be
used for a 65536-frame block.

The crossfeed rebuild condition requires either long convolver (instead of
both, which rebuilt all four convolvers on every enable) and the process
path reads the crossfeed mode once per block (instead of per sample, which
could index bs2b[] - two entries - with values 2 to 5 and write filter
state over the following DDC and convolver fields), ported from the same
repository.

Engine file provenance (U-5)
----------------------------
Files:
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/bs2b.c
  app/src/main/cpp/libjamesdsp/Main/libjamesdsp/jni/jamesdsp/jdsp/Effects/eel2/numericSys/FFTConvolver.c

Neither file carries a license header. bs2b.c implements the Bauer
stereophonic-to-binaural DSP by Boris Mikhaylov (libbs2b, dual-licensed
GPL-2.0-or-later / MIT), C-ported inside JamesDSPLib. FFTConvolver.c
derives from the FFTConvolver library by Christian Schoenebeck
(HiFi-LoFi, MIT), rewritten in JamesDSPLib against the EEL2 FFT. Both
lineages are compatible with this repository's GPL-3.0; this notice
records the attribution.

Additionally, the unsigned-wrap guard on the convolution segment remainders
(remaining = i * blockSize >= irLen ? 0 : irLen - i * blockSize, applied at
all segment-copy sites) and the segment-count consistency check before
FFTConvolver2x2RefreshImpulseResponse in arbEqConv.c follow the idiom of
RootlessViPER4Android, https://github.com/alienware377/RootlessViPER4Android
(which applies it at four of the sites; this repository applies it at all of
them).

